2026-11-28 04:26:31,003 - INFO - [MainThread] - Received claude code message: {'content': [{'tool_use_id': 'call-a6716a992fe344e48c33a3c6e1abc8b0', 'content': '### S01-E4-R1\n0 Read /app/build.py\n1 Bash Inspect checkpoint files and Blender installation\n4 Edit /app/build.py\n5 Bash Render both chair contact candidates\n8 Read /app/candidate_a.png\n9 Read /app/candidate_b.png\n10 Bash Measure every caster against local floor and render side views\n14 Read /app/candidate_a_side.png\n15 Read /app/candidate_b_side.png\n18 Edit /app/build.py\n19 Bash Render revised camera and grounded casters\n22 Read /app/final.png\n23 Bash Verify final wheel contact and chair heights\n26 TEXT Delivered the editable reconstruction and render:\n\n- `/app/build.py`\n- `/app/scene.blend`\n- `/app/final.png` (640 × 360)\n\nI compared lowering the complete chairs with revising the caster geometry, and chose the revised casters to preserve seat height and better match the reference silhouette. Evaluated-geometry checks found all ten wheels at the local floor surface; side views were used to inspect the assemblies and connections.\n\n### S01-E4-R2\n0 Bash Inspect checkpoint files and Blender availability\n1 Read /app/build.py\n4 Bash Preserve the original scene checkpoint\n5 Edit /app/build.py\n6 Edit /app/build.py\n7 Edit /app/build.py\n12 Bash Render both chair contact candidates\n14 Read /app/whole.png\n15 Read /app/caster.png\n16 Write /app/check_chairs.py\n17 Bash Measure every wheel against the floor and render side views\n22 Read /app/whole_check.log\n23 Read /app/caster_check.log\n24 Read /app/whole_side.png\n25 Read /app/scene_side.png\n30 Edit /app/build.py\n31 Edit /app/build.py\n32 Edit /app/build.py\n33 Bash Render revised viewpoint and materials\n38 Read /app/final.png\n40 Edit /app/build.py\n41 Bash Render adjusted scene framing\n44 Read /app/final.png\n46 TEXT Completed the editable reconstruction and rendered it at 640 × 360:\n\n- `/app/build.py` — executable Blender Python source\n- `/app/scene.blend` — editable scene\n- `/app/final.png` — final render\n\nI compared both chair-contact candidates using evaluated wheel geometry and side renders. Both brought all ten wheels to the floor without measured penetration. The selected caster revision retains the original seat height and gives the wheels a rounder silhouette closer to the reference than lowering the original flat-oriented cylinders.\n\n### S02-E4-R1\n0 Read /app/build.py\n1 Bash Inspect checkpoint files\n4 Bash Check the Blender installation\n6 Bash Render two fixed-camera door swing candidates\n8 Read /app/candidate_a.png\n9 Read /app/candidate_b.png\n12 Bash Render a revised coherent door assembly\n13 Bash Render a top-view visibility diagnostic\n16 Read /app/candidate_c.png\n17 Read /app/diagnostic_top.png\n20 Bash Render door moved forward for comparison\n21 Bash Inspect revised doorway from above\n24 Read /app/candidate_d.png\n25 Read /app/candidate_c_top.png\n28 Bash Render a right-wall hinged door candidate\n30 Read /app/candidate_e.png\n32 Bash Render another right-wall door swing\n34 Read /app/candidate_f.png\n36 Bash Render the corrected right-wall door face\n38 Read /app/test_final.png\n40 Bash Build and render the revised editable scene\n41 Bash Render side view to inspect door assembly\n44 Read /app/final.png\n45 Read /app/diagnostic_side.png\n48 Bash Compare a closer doorway at the fixed camera\n50 Read /app/candidate_g.png\n52 TEXT The revised scene and render are available:\n\n- [Executable Blender source](/app/build.py)\n- [Editable Blender scene](/app/scene.blend)\n- [Final render, 640 × 360](/app/final.png)\n\nI compared fixed-camera door-swing and relocated-hinge candidates. The selected version shows the paneled door face, though its placement and the surrounding doorway still differ from the reference. The side diagnostic was obstructed by the wall, so it did not conclusively verify intersections or hinge alignment.\n\n### S02-E4-R2\n0 Read /app/build.py\n1